   "status": "One provisional brand mark, the MrDemonWolf, Inc. studio logo (two mascot images rendered from company brand files and the boot splash image rendered from the logo screen; company branding, all rights reserved), three provisional character images (redrawn 2026-10-08; full-size masters under apps/game/art-source/characters/ and the downscaled copies the game loads) and the engineer's two-frame crank pose cut from their sprite (2026-10-14), one title background, three layered gameplay rooms (far, mid and near plates for the corridor, Records Access and the Service Junction), sixteen station prop images (seven for the corridor and Records Access; six for the Service Junction plus one documented derivative crop of its tank; the junction reuses the corridor breaker), five door-end atlases, each a cross-wall turned across the walkway with its doorway transparent (the corridor seal's, 2026-10-12: the cross-wall, rolling steel door, near column, camera, lamp glass and bypass handwheel; 2026-10-14: with the steel blast frame, RESTRICTED AREA plate, inner blast leaf and clean cutaway; Records Access's two swing doors, 2026-10-13: both cross-walls, the steel leaves' faces and edge, the near columns and stubs, the security container and the status lamps' glass; the Service Junction blast door's, 2026-10-13: the doorway, the cross-wall, the leaf whole, breaking and thrown, the near column whole and blown, the blast damage, the release bay, the stub and the lamp glass; the Service Junction entry's swing door, 2026-10-13: the cross-wall, the leaf's faces and edge, the near column, the stub and the lamp glass; and the Service Junction exit door's, 2026-10-13: the cross-wall, sliding steel leaf, exit bolt housing, status lamp glass and the service passage beyond), the corridor's two caged red beacons in one atlas (2026-10-14), two sentry images, three derivative marketing captures, the Roboto and Montserrat font families with their licence texts, four project-written font and theme resources (three FontVariation .tres files and the UI theme), three project shader files, one generated changelog text export, one procedural sound-effect set (code, no files) and seven processed CC0 sound recordings (the Service Junction's three pressure-line loops, relief-vent burst and coolant-cloud bed from Joseph Sardin's BigSoundBank recordings, and WOLF's seam and refusal growls from OpenGameArt recordings) recorded. Glows, haze, dust, the Records Access and Service Junction lockdown beacons, reflections, particles, the Service Junction's state overlays (gauge needle, vent and door-lamp glows, panel lights, the station name plates, floor mark, arm rods and cable, the sentry's beam and eye light), the swing doors' leaves (meshes over their atlas regions, lit per vertex) and the screen grade are procedural built-in nodes and three small shaders (the registered reflection and grade shader files plus the valve wheel's inline disc mask), not image assets. Godot's .import and .uid sidecar files and this manifest itself are not registered.",
